1 NOTE {geni:about_me} Bjarne Grimstvedt his visit to Iowa in 1944 by his daughter Grete Syre: He had a wife Svanhild and two children, Terje born 1935 and Kjell born in 1939. The last time he saw his family before the war started was in
2 CONC  August/September 1939. The next time was autumn of 1945. All these years he was on board the same ship ÒIda Bakke fro Haugesund. When Norway was occupied in April 1940 they were in Pacfic Ocean. The connections with his family we
2 CONC nt through the Internatinal Red Cross and was limited to some few words. He then thought of his mother's letter to America and he remembered the names of his uncles Albert, Ed and Severin. HIs mother had written to Ed Askeland, Th
2 CONC or, Iowa, and now he wrote a letter to the same address. Some days later he got a letter from his daughter Sarah Wooster. They corresponded all through the war. In 1944 the ship was in New York and would be there for some weeks, a
2 CONC nd he had to go away from the ship for awhile. Sarah had asked him to come to Iowa several times and he now decided to take the train without telling anybody. He went off the train at a station called Ames He was tired and booked 
2 CONC into a hotel and fell asleep. He woke up the next afternnon and noticed there was a telephone. He had no telephone number but remembered that Sarah worked at Marten Grocery Store in Eagle Grove, Iowa. It took some minutes, then he
2 CONC  got an answer He asked for Sarah Wooster, and she said " It is me". They agreed Bjarne should take a taxi to Thor the following morning. After having spoken to Bjarne thought the taxi couldn't get enough gasoline to drive him so 
2 CONC far. There were rations on petrol, sho she got help from family, and she and another got a car and some gasoline and drove to Ames, Iowa. My father was just leaving the hotel when these two girls came towards him. He immediately r
2 CONC ecognized one of them. She looked much like his sister Sigrid. Sarah had informed some the family that he was coming, but they were told not to say anything to her father. He was out in the field when they came, Bjarne went up to 
2 CONC his uncle. He immiediately knew who he was, he looked just just like his father. He spent two weeks with the famiy. He met them all, his mother's uncle Reinart and his uncles Albert, Severin and Eliseus (Ed). Reinart was the time 
2 CONC almost 80 years old and he wanted a longorv to cut the grass. Back in Norway my father was in Tysvaer and told his folks about this, and they sent it. He stayed some days at his uncle Ed's place, and the rest at his uncle Albert's
2 CONC  place. His uncle Albert hadn't had a holiday since he had come to America, but when Bjarne, came he took free from his own business all the time. One of his daughters worked at a local radio station, and every day she sent a gree
2 CONC ting to her cousin on the air. They also had a family-party in the park in Eagle Grove were a lot of Askeland people were gathered.
