1 NAME Johannes Olsen /Frantsen/
2 GIVN Johannes Olsen
2 _MARNM Frantsen
1 SEX M
1 BIRT
2 DATE 18 JAN 1849
2 PLAC Haukås
2 ADDR
3 STAE Rogaland
3 CTRY Norway
1 DEAT
2 DATE 22 JUN 1918
2 ADDR
3 CITY Knysna
3 CTRY South Africa
1 OCCU
1 NOTE {geni:about_me} Moved to Stavanger in 1856, at the age of 7. 
2 CONT
2 CONT Johannes Olsen was the son of Ole Frantzsen who was the brother of Lars, the father of Johannes, Frank, Karen and Ingeborg. He was born in Norway (Haukås i Tysvær, Rogaland) and decided to follow his cousins, Johannes and Frank to
2 CONC  South Africa in about 1885 at the request of the Thesens. He was a skilled shipbuilder and managed the Thesen`s sawmills before the discovery of gold in Millwood.
2 CONT
2 CONT He left his wife Anne Serine and three children in Norway and sent for them in 1887 when he felt he could provide for them. He lived with Frank and Martha in their Millwood home in the Knysna forest until his wife and family arriv
2 CONC ed from Norway. He worked for many years for messrs Thesen. His son Olaf Ferdinand distinguished himself in the Knysna High School and later as a businessman in Knysna.
2 CONT
2 CONT Johannes died when he was 70 years old. A very complimentary obituary was published in the Knysna Mail on the 25 June 1918.
2 CONT
2 CONT Both Johannes and Anne are buried in Knysna.
