1 NAME Della Gladys /Hodgdon/
2 GIVN Della Gladys
2 SURN Hodgdon
2 _MARNM Roseland
1 SEX F
1 BIRT
2 DATE 25 AUG 1877
2 ADDR
3 STAE Iowa
3 CTRY United States
1 DEAT
2 DATE 17 JUL 1948
2 ADDR
3 CITY Paullina
3 STAE Iowa
3 CTRY United States
1 NOTE {geni:about_me} Mrs. Samuel Roseland Dies After Long Illness-Buried Monday
2 CONT
2 CONT Mrs. Samuel Roseland died at her home here last Saturday morning, July 17, of an illness that had kept her confined for the past 13 years and in a critical condition for over four months. She would have attained her 71st birthday 
2 CONC August 25.
2 CONT
2 CONT Rev. L. R. Middents officiated at funeral services held Monday afternoon. A short service was held at the home at which Mrs Ida Chamness, West Branch, sister of Samuel Roseland, offered a prayer. Services were held at the Presbyte
2 CONC rian church at 2 o'clock. Mrs. Matt Shankland and Frances Smith sang "Rock of Ages" and "The Old Rugged Cross " Mrs. Robert Livingston was organist The pallbearers were Glen Chase, Orville Hatfield, Justin Ginger, Ina Dornbusch, J
2 CONC r., Howard Tjossem and Matt Shankland. 
2 CONT
2 CONT Burial took place in Prairie View cemetery. 
2 CONT
2 CONT Born August 25, 1877, Delia Gladys Hodgdon, was a daughter of Charles and Ada Hodgdon. On December 8, 1895 she was married to Samuel Roseland They made their home in Paullina during their entire married life. Mrs. Roseland became 
2 CONC a member of the Presbyterian church here on February 2, 1919.
2 CONT
2 CONT Mrs. Roseland is survived by three daughters, Mrs. J. M. Adams, St. Louis, Mo., Mrs. Arthur Kastman and Mrs. J. C. Lange, Jr., Paullina. Also four sons, Paul, San Gabriel, Calif.; John, Clear Lake; George, Paullina and Charles of 
2 CONC Clear Lake. 
2 CONT
2 CONT She is also survived by a sister, Mrs. William Puhrman and five brothers, Harry, John, Myles, Delbert and Burdette Hodgdon. 
2 CONT
2 CONT Relatives from a distance to attend the services were: Mrs. Ida Chamness and daughter, Pauline, of West Branch, Mr. and Mrs. Arna Uuskallia and daughter, Pauline, of West Branch; Mr. and Mrs. John Hodgdon and daughters, Patty and 
2 CONC Marlys Ann, of Quimby; Mrs. William Puhrmann and son, Bradley, of Charles City; Mr. and Mrs. Fell, Washta and Mr. and Mrs. Harry Hodgdon, Mr. and Mrs. Marvin Kish, Mrs. Bert Castle, all of Sioux Falls. 
2 CONT
2 CONT Others from out of town were: Mrs. Beda Kastman and Don Prohoska of Omaha; Mr and Mrs. A. E. Eddy, Mrs. R. E. Nelson, Mrs. Guy Wisguhf and Mr. and Mrs. Ray KruzzeL all of Clear Lake; Earl Thomson, Cherokee, and Mr. and Mrs. Alvin 
2 CONC Goodmanson, Sanborn.
2 CONT
2 CONT Paullina Times, Paullina, Iowa, July 22, 1948, p1
2 CONT
