1 NOTE {geni:about_me} Joseph, Floys father, owned a restaurant in Paullina. John Tobias worked there to earn mony to attend college.
2 CONT
2 CONT John and Floy attended college in Cedar Falls Iowa, where they married in 1924. They were teachers. They returned to Paullina after college, then John accepted a teaching job at Hartley Iowa (near Paullina), where John Samuel was 
2 CONC born. John then moved his growing family to Clear Lake Iowa where he taught geometry and was the football coach at Clear Lake High School. John Tobias was a businessman in addition to being a teacher. With Verlee's husband Guy Wis
2 CONC gerhof, John Tobias owned The Corner Drug Store in Clear Lake. Guy was the pharmacist and John was the manager. John bought 2 farms near Clear Lake. Unrelated families lived and worked on them but he loved the land and was active 
2 CONC in the farms' work and management.
