1 NOTE {geni:about_me} Husband of Evelyn Parents of Sam, Mary, Margaret, Steve, Nancy, Carol, Wanda and Gayle
2 CONT
2 CONT Services held for H. George Roseland
2 CONT
2 CONT Funeral services >for H. George Roseland were held Monday, February 12, 1996, at 10:30 a.m. at the Gaudian-Eldndge Funeral Home' in Paullina, Iowa, with Rev. Daniel B. Quinn officiating. The casket bearers were Dick Halstrom, Orly
2 CONC nn Strampe, Jim Ryan, Cliff Hellmann, Jim Fritz and Jeff Ryan. Interment was at Prairie View Cemetery in Paullina, Iowa, under the direction of the Gaudian-Eldridge Funeral Home 
2 CONT
2 CONT OBITUARY 
2 CONT
2 CONT H. George Roseland, the son of Sam and Delia Hodgdon Roseland, was born March 19, 1903, in O'Brien County, Iowa. He received his education in Paullina schools. 
2 CONT
2 CONT He was united in marriage to Faye Boatman and later united in marriage to Evelyn Ryan Brownmiller. 
2 CONT
2 CONT For fifty-three years, he owned and operated his own trucking business. He passed away on Friday, February 9, 1996, at Millies Rest Home in Sutherland reaching the age of ninety-two years, ten months and twenty days. 
2 CONT
2 CONT George leaves to cherish his memory to his wife, Evelyn of Paullina; children: Sam Roseland of Inwood, Mary Bruns of Paullina, Steve Roseland of Rock Valley, Nancy Brownmiller of Milwaukee, Wisconsin, Carol Axdahl of Paullina and 
2 CONC Gayle Roseland of Boone; twenty-one grandchildren: [redacted]; several great-grandchildren; one sister, Bernice Lange of Paullina; a sister-in-law, Helen Roseland of Clear Lake; also a host of other relatives and friends. 
2 CONT
2 CONT He was preceded in death by two daughters, Margaret and Wanda; his parents; two sisters, Ada and Mabel; three brothers, Charles, John and Paul, and grandson, Dennis Axdahl.
2 CONT
2 CONT Paullina Times, Paullina, Iowa, February 15, 1996, p3
2 CONT
