1 NOTE {geni:about_me} Funeral services for Ada Roseland Kastman were held at 1:00 p.m. Tuesday, December 8, 1992, at the Gaudian-Eldridge Funeral Home in Paullina, Iowa, with Rev. Reuben Tjaden officiating. The pallbearers were Jack Mau
2 CONC , Steve Louscher, Bee Maytum, Don Dawson. Ken Pauling and Merle Ihle. Interment was at Prairie View Cemetery, Paullina, Iowa, under the care of the Gaudian-Eldridge Funeral Home of Paullina. 
2 CONT
2 CONT OBITUARY 
2 CONT
2 CONT Ada Kastman, the daughter of Samuel and Delia Hodgdon Roseland, was born June 30, 1906, in O'Brien County, Iowa. She moved as a child to Paullina and received her elementary and secondary schooling in the Paullina Public Schools. 
2 CONC After receiving her teaching certificate at the University of Omaha in 1927, she taught for many years in the Akron, Iowa, elementary school. 
2 CONT
2 CONT She married Art Kastman in Omaha in 1943. In 1946, she and her husband entered into a partnership in the operation of Lange's Cafe in Paullina. After the termination of the partnership, she continued to work at the cafe until her 
2 CONC retirement in 1975. She passed away Saturday, December 5,1992, at the Wide View Rest Home in Paullina, reaching the age of 86 years, 5 months and 5 days.
2 CONT
2 CONT She was a long time member of the Presbyterian Church. Ada leaves to cherish her memory her husband Art of Paullina; one brother George Roseland, one sister, Bernice Lange, both of Paullina. She was preceded in death by her parent
2 CONC s; brothers: Paul, John and Charles; and one sister, Mrs. Mabel Adams.
2 CONT
2 CONT Paullina Times, Paullina, Iowa, December 10, 1992, P3 
