1 NOTE {geni:about_me} Gladys Outland Bailey, 86, Barnesville, Ohio, died Wednesday, in Fairfax, VA. She was born February 9, 1917, in her beloved state of Iowa, daughter of the late Howard and Jergina Pauline Roiseland Outland. She earn
2 CONC ed a B. S. degree in Education from Ohio University and taught in Barnesville Schools for several years. She was a member of Stillwater Friends Meeting and was very active in many local organizations. She was preceeded in death by
2 CONC  her first husband, Lester W Bailey, and her second husband, H B Rhodes; three brothers and one sister. Surviving are her husband, Nathan Bailey of Bolivar, Ohio; three daughters, Bonnie J Bailey of S Riding, VA, Mrs Delmar (Jane)
2 CONC  Gregg of Quaker City, Ohio, and Mrs Dan (Judith Ann) Hoffman of Columbus, Ohio; step-children, Dent and Patricia and Beverly and Marilyn and families; six grandchildren; five great-grandchildren; many neices and nephews; and all 
2 CONC her friends at Walton Home. Friends will be received from 4 to 9 PM on Saturday at the Campbell-Plumly-Milburn Funeral Home, 319 N Chestnut Street, Barnesville, Ohio, where services will be held at 2 PM on Sunday at Stillwater Fri
2 CONC ends Meeting After the Manner of Friends. Burial will follow in Stillwater Cemetery, Barnesville, Ohio. Memorial contributions would be welcome to: Unverferth House, 190 King Avenue, Columbus, Ohio, 43201. 
2 CONT
