1 NOTE {geni:about_me} Etnesoga IV page 220 Austrheim (59b), (60), Etnesoga V page 104 Bjørk (6), page 99 Trongjo u. Lunda (23), page 220 Flokatveit (39), page 91 Veien u. Lussnes (31), page 99 Trongjo u. Lunda (23).
2 CONT
2 CONT Census 1865 Lindevig, Etne: https://www.digitalarkivet.no/census/person/pf01038223001225
2 CONT
2 CONT Sjur og Margrethe took over his father's farm in Austrheim, but had to sell in 1847, after which they moved to Bjørk. In the fall of 1850 they also had to sell the farm in Bjørk. Almost the entire sum was spent covering his debt. 
2 CONC In 1851 Sjur and Margrethe settled down in Trongjo on the Lunda farm where Margrethe came from. Around 1858 they moved to Flokatveit and in the early 1860's to Lussnes. Their home was close to Lindevik and was called "Vegen" (The 
2 CONC Road) because it was close to the country road. Probably little or no land was included in their property. After some years Sjur tore down their house and moved once again, this time back to Trongjo on the Lunda farm. After Sjur d
2 CONC ied in 1883, Margrethe moved in 1884 to her children in Illinois, USA.
