1 NAME Olaf Ferdinand /Frantsen/
2 GIVN Olaf Ferdinand
2 SURN Frantsen
2 _MARNM Franzsen
1 SEX M
1 BIRT
2 DATE 15 JUL 1876
2 ADDR
3 CITY Stavanger
3 STAE Rogaland
3 CTRY Norway
1 BAPM
2 DATE 6 AUG 1876
2 ADDR
3 CITY Domkirken, Stavanger
3 STAE Rogaland
3 CTRY Norway
1 DEAT
2 DATE 27 JAN 1932
2 ADDR
3 CITY Knysna
3 STAE Western Cape
3 CTRY South Africa
1 OCCU
1 NOTE {geni:about_me} Olaf was the eldest son of Johannes Olsen Franzsen. He arrived with his mother and his siblings in Knysna from Norway when he was about 12 years old. After the death of his father-in-law, Mr. James Scott, Olaf`s wi
2 CONC fe, Agnes inherited the business and Olaf then combined his own business with that of his wife. He was named for a number of years in the South African Who`s Who in business as a dealer in wood and a general dealer. Olaf was a ver
2 CONC y well respected citizen and businessman in Knysna and when he died, an obituary was published in the Knysna Advertiser on Friday 5th 1932. Another obituary as follows was published but the source is unknown.
2 CONT
2 CONT "On wednesday of last week the death occured with suddeness of Mr. Olaf Franzsen. The deceased gentleman, who was very highly respected in Knysna, had not complained of any particular indisposition and had gone about his ordinary 
2 CONC daily duties in his usual manner. Mrs. Franzsen had gone to George as it is clear that there was at the moment no reason to think that his health was likely to cause any immediate apprehension. On the previous day Mr Franzsen had 
2 CONC spent the evening at the house of relatives, retiring to bed at a moderately early hour. The next morning, Wednesday, he was up and about fairly early and about 7 am, after clearing his private boz at the Post Office, he took a cu
2 CONC p of coffee on the stoep of his friends house. He then visited the store and furniture factory and at 7:45 am he went up to his own house for breakfast. According to the maidservant`s  account, she took in the usual porridge and p
2 CONC laced it on the table, returning to the kitchen to prepare an omelet and to await the dinig room bell. But as apparently an unusually long time elapsed, she went to the dining romm and looked in at the door. Mr. Franzsen was recli
2 CONC ning on a coach, so beeing alarmed at this unusual procedure she immediately ran out and informed a near neighbour who in turn telephoned for a  Doctor and then rushed  to the house only to find however that the poor fellow had pa
2 CONC ssed away. The funeral was held the next day at the Wesleyan Church and in the absence of the Revd. Mr Owen who is away in Synod, the service was taken by the rector of the parish, the Revd. Canon Thornely Jones. The great respect
2 CONC  in which the deceased gentleman was held and the real grief at the passing of so kindly a soul was shown by the enormous affendance at the funeral. There is many a poor brother in the Knysna district who will miss the kindly char
2 CONC ity and benevolence of Olaf Franzsen. Our deepest symphaties go out to his bereaved family"
1 FAMC @F6000000008173775368@
1 RFN geni:6000000006187224891
1 SUBM @S6000000000699386666@
1 CHAN
2 DATE 23 APR 2020
