1 NAME Hugh Erling /Franzsen/
2 GIVN Hugh Erling
2 _MARNM Franzsen
1 NAME Hugh Erling Franzsen
1 SEX M
1 BIRT
2 DATE 6 DEC 1892
2 ADDR
3 CITY Knysna
3 STAE WC
3 CTRY South Africa
1 DEAT
2 DATE 12 JUL 1964
2 ADDR
3 CITY Germiston
3 STAE GP
3 POST 1609
3 CTRY South Africa
1 NOTE {geni:about_me} Hugh Franzsen, went mostly by his middle name of Erling. He signed up with his 3 brothers for military service during WW1. in 1914. He was the only one to come home again. The monument in Knysna bears the names of 
2 CONC his deceased brothers. The oldest brother, Harold was courting the local School Teacher, Ellie Staples when he went to war. After his death she was courted by Hugh Erling and they married, and were dedicated followers of Jesus. 
2 CONT
2 CONT After WW1 H. Earling Franzsen worked for the Victoria Falls Power Supply, later it became Electricity Supply Commission (ESCOM) and he retired from that job after 35 years service. He took a break to serve again in WW2 but did not
2 CONC  see overseas service. He spent a year or more breaking in horses for the Cavalry in Pretoria, then returned to ESCOM.
1 FAMC @F6000000005997893211@
1 RFN geni:6000000005953854235
