2 CONT
2 CONT Halvor, Martha, and Erick left Tysvaer Parish on 8 Apr 1857 for America, likely arriving at the port of Quebec.  On arrival, they headed for Koshkonong a Norwegian immigrant center near Cambridge, WI.  On 25 Oct 1858, Halvor becam
2 CONC e a citizen.  He moved his family via covered wagon to South Dakota, arriving on 1 Aug 1861.  They were poor, but worked hard.  By 1871, his land contained 3 houses, 4 stables, 2 sheds, and a granery.
